WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.860
Critics of Bentham had a sharp jibe.

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:07.860
If all pleasures are equal, his was
a doctrine worthy only of swine.

3
00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:11.140
John Stuart Mill was
raised as a utilitarian.

4
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.030
He set out to answer them.

5
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.940
In 1859, in On Liberty, he asked when
power can rightfully be used over a person.

6
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.340
Are some pleasures worth more than others,

7
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.840
and when may society
stop you chasing yours?

8
00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.500
In this mission, you'll see how
Mill took on the swine objection,

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.190
and what it cost him.

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.330
Then you'll test his harm
principle on real laws,

11
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.730
and compare 2 kinds of
rule utilitarianism.

12
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.120
Your mission: weigh up whether
pleasures differ in worth,

13
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.230
and when society may step in.
